<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: LITHUANIA-CZECH CSOB OKAYS LOAN TO STATE COMMERCIAL BANK.</title>
<headline>LITHUANIA-CZECH CSOB OKAYS LOAN TO STATE COMMERCIAL BANK.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech state-controlled Ceskoslovenska Obchodni Banka said on Tuesday it had concluded a $30 million loan agreement with the State Commercial Bank of Lithuania.</p>
<p>In a statement, CSOB's spokesman Milan Tomanek said the money would go toward financing Czech exports to Lithuania.</p>
<p>Last year, CSOB provided financing for the purchase of 28 articulated buses and 40 trolleybuses for transport in the Lithuanian capital city of Vilnius and the city of Kaunas.</p>
<p>No further details were immediately available.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
